  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1225 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nWarm advection mid clouds developing on satellite, and forecast in \nsoundings/NBM sky cover. Only about 50mb thickness at around 700mb, \nso will have a limited impact on the forecast aside from less than \nfull sunshine for some locations in the east today. Local downslope \nconditions for a brief period tonight with BUFKIT profiles \nindicating about 40kts in the critical layer, and it will take just \nbefore the front coming through, when we briefly achieve a southwest \noriented wind, to really take effect. Otherwise just breezy with \nsouth flow and 1/2km winds at about 25-30kts. \n\nTuesday will be dominated by weak low level flow and weak cold \nadvection, with enhanced mixing on a northwest wind component. NBM \nhighs around 80.\n\nThe rest of the week remains mild albeit not quite as above normal \nas the pattern is dominated by a northwesterly flow regime.\n\nFor the weekend, currently deterministic EC/GFS/Canadian all depict \nsome form of ridge crosses the north central CONUS followed by a \ndeepening trough over the western CONUS. Southwest flow regime will \nhelp generate a low over the northern Rockies followed by a frontal \npassage. Starting to see some NBM POPs creep into Sat/Sun but its \nstill pretty far off to come to any final conclusions regarding the \nweekend forecast.",
